     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I don't doubt your authority to prescribe it. The problem is that 5100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, with no established benefit and a real risk of lactic acidosis. A quick \"confirm\" is also how a units or per-day vs. per-dose mix-up usually gets through, so I'd rather stop it here than send it to the patient.\n\nThere are two ways forward:\n\n1. **If there's a deliberate clinical reason** for this dose, such as a research protocol or a specialist recommendation, tell me what it is. I'll enter the order with that reason in the note and flag it for pharmacist verification before it's given.\n2. **If the intended total was 1700 mg or 2550 mg per day**, I can enter 850 mg twice daily or 850 mg three times daily with meals right away.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
